dence mapping records a Lean proof of exactly this statement. Lean status per paper is kept in authored/evidence-status.json.","citation_ids":["cite.long.thm-257-logarithmic-counterexample"],"evidence_ids":["mapping.long.thm-257-logarithmic-counterexample"],"id":"long.thm-257-logarithmic-counterexample","kind":"claim","label":"Long record Theorem 13.1 (arithmetic logarithmic counterexample)","locator":"Long record Theorem 13.1, p. 142, label thm:257-logarithmic-counterexample","source_id":"paper.long.pdf","statement":"*For every integer $H\\ge2$ and every real $A_0\\ge0$, there are a squarefree positive integer $L$ and a finite nonempty set $F$ of distinct squarefree positive integers such that\n$$\n\\min F>\\max\\{L,A_0\\},\\qquad\n \\kappa_1(F;1)\\le\\frac{30\\log2}{H},\\qquad\n \\mathbb P_L(U_F>1)\\ge1-e^{-1}.\n$$\nFor these $F,L$, some $R\\ge0$ satisfies $\\mathscr D_{L;R,L}\\mathbf1_{\\{U_F>1\\}}>1/2$. Consequently, no absolute constant $C$ satisfies\n$$\n\n \\mathscr D_{L;R,M}\\mathbf1_{\\{U_F>t\\}}\n \\le C(1+L/M)\\kappa_1(F;t)\n \\tag{E}\n$$\nuniformly in finite $F$, positive integers $L,M$, integers $R\\ge0$, and $0<t\\le1$.*","status":"unverified"},"ref":"sha256:f31aeb6174afd909393ada9bc329cd29dc9b1b6a0de8f72a49f18ab372947af5/nodes/long.thm-257-logarithmic-counterexample","relations":[{"derived":false,"family":"arguments","from":"sha256:f31aeb6174afd909393ada9bc329cd29dc9b1b6a0de8f72a49f18ab372947af5/nodes/long.thm-257-logarithmic-counterexample","id":"sha256:f31aeb6174afd909393ada9bc329cd29dc9b1b6a0de8f72a49f18ab372947af5/edges/%5B%22long.thm-257-logarithmic-counterexample%22%2C%22lean.ErdosProblems.Erdos257.PaperCompleteR21.arithmetic_logarithmic_counterexample%22%2C%22formalizes%22%5D","kind":"formalizes","record_ref":"sha256:f31aeb6174afd909393ada9bc329cd29dc9b1b6a0de8f72a49f18ab372947af5/edges/%5B%22long.thm-257-logarithmic-counterexample%22%2C%22lean.ErdosProblems.Erdos257.PaperCompleteR21.arithmetic_logarithmic_counterexample%22%2C%22formalizes%22%5